Manage recon targets, profiles, scans, and findings.

Every recon command talks to the running usulnet server over the
local API. Configure the server via --server or $USULNET_API_URL,
and authenticate via $USULNET_API_TOKEN.

Usage:
  usulnet recon [flags]
  usulnet recon [command]

Available Commands:
  findings    Browse findings produced by completed scans
  profile     List the predefined scan profiles available to targets
  scan        Start, list, watch, cancel, or download recon scan reports
  target      Register, list, or verify ownership of recon targets

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for recon
      --server string   usulnet API URL (default $USULNET_API_URL)
      --token string    API token (default $USULNET_API_TOKEN)

Global Flags:
  -c, --config string   config file path (default: /etc/usulnet/config.yaml or ./config.yaml)
      --json            shortcut for --output json (overrides --output)
      --output string   output format: table|json|yaml (default "table")
  -q, --quiet           suppress informational output (errors and primary data still print)

Use "usulnet recon [command] --help" for more information about a command.
